[00000] A British farmer is right to ask why the British beef industry was visible by its absence. Symbolism matters; so do British producers. Number 10 made the choice; the President noticed; British beef will be on every other state banquet menu this year, and the rural sector deserves that assurance.
[00001] By the word I used, yes. Crossings have not stopped, and pretending otherwise would be worse than accepting the verbatim test. The returns agreement, the processing reform, and the gang enforcement are the three levers that move the number, and I will be judged on whether they do.
[00002] "Prime Minister. I am hearing reports that Britain is considering unilateral recognition of a Palestinian state. I need you to hear this clearly: any such move would be the most serious rupture in the bilateral relationship since 1956. We will recall our ambassador. We will review every cooperation agreement. Is this really the legacy you want?"
[00003] "Prime Minister, I have seen your Foreign Secretary's statement on freedom of navigation in the Taiwan Strait. I want to be direct: what you call freedom of navigation we regard as a provocation. China's position on Taiwan is non-negotiable. I expect Britain to stay out of this."
