[00005] Pieter van der Berg is calling. "Prime Minister, I want to speak frankly. Several allies have asked me to raise the UK's defence spending trajectory. At current projections you will fall below 2% by next year. I need to be able to tell them this will not happen."
[00006] "Prime Minister. This year's Hajj season is approaching. 25,000 British Muslims will travel. We would like to coordinate quietly on visa logistics, consular access, and any safeguarding concerns. A small gesture goes a long way with your Muslim communities."
[00007] "Prime Minister, Russia has been testing our Arctic sovereignty claims. We're strengthening our northern position but I want Five Eyes coordination. A joint UK-Canada statement on Arctic freedom of navigation would help our domestic political situation and signal Allied resolve."
[00008] "Prime Minister. Russia has cut all remaining gas supply via the Nord Stream replacement route. German industry is at risk this winter. We need either UK LNG via Milford Haven, or a guarantee of UK electricity exports via the interconnectors. Either way, we will reciprocate when our position is reversed."
