[00223] Constructing the UK's largest energy storage facility in the Scottish Highlands, capable of storing 30 gigawatt-hours of electricity by pumping water between two reservoirs. When renewable supply exceeds demand, surplus electricity fills the upper reservoir; during peak demand, water is released through turbines. The project resolves a critical grid balancing challenge as wind and solar dominate the generation mix.
