[00243] Demolishing and rebuilding 500 schools across England that contain RAAC concrete or are otherwise assessed as structurally unsound, creating modern learning environments with excellent acoustics, heating, air quality, and digital infrastructure. Over 1.3 million pupils currently study in buildings with serious structural deficiencies. Programme prioritises areas of high deprivation.
[00244] Deploying 100 Galleri blood test machines across the NHS to enable multi-cancer early detection from a single blood draw, alongside a major expansion of mobile mammography, colonoscopy, and CT scanning capacity. Catching cancer at stage 1 rather than stage 4 increases five-year survival rates from 20% to 90% and dramatically reduces treatment costs.
[00245] Deploying a layered air defence network including Sky Sabre missiles, counter-drone systems, and hardened radar installations to protect UK critical national infrastructure from drone and cruise missile attacks. The Ukraine war demonstrated that cheap drones can defeat expensive military equipment. The UK has major gaps in its low-level air defence architecture.
[00246] Deploying five small modular reactors (SMRs) at brownfield sites across the UK under a government-backed programme with Rolls-Royce as the lead manufacturer. Each SMR produces 470 megawatts of zero-carbon electricity and can be factory-built in three years rather than the decade needed for conventional nuclear. The programme targets export potential alongside domestic energy security.
[00247] Designating and building five new garden cities across England, each of between 30,000 and 80,000 homes, modelled on Ebenezer Howard's principles of green space, mixed use, and community ownership of land. Sites are chosen near existing transport corridors including East Hemel, Tempsford, Melton, Thetford, and Cannock. The programme targets 250,000 new homes by the end of the decade.
[00248] Detailed disclosure of cyber incidents can compromise the methods and sources used to detect them, and the agencies have to make a judgement between public information and operational effectiveness. That judgement is reviewed regularly by the Intelligence and Security Committee.
[00249] Digital transformation in social care follows the market maturity of the underlying products, and mandating national procurement before the vendor landscape is ready risks locking the sector into first-generation solutions. Slow procurement can be the right answer when the technology is still evolving.
