[00264] Establishes the elected second chamber the referendum mandated: a Senate of the Nations and Regions with members elected by proportional list, defined powers over revising and delaying legislation, and guaranteed representation for every nation and region.
[00265] Establishing a centre of excellence for national cyber defence, incident response, and skills development in Manchester, co-located with GCHQ's northern hub. The centre will coordinate the government's response to major cyberattacks and provide support to critical infrastructure operators and NHS trusts. The UK faces over 100 significant cyber incidents annually targeting public services.
[00266] Every Active Travel England target was set in this Parliament, every funding round was opened in this Parliament, and the 3,000-mile completion certificate was signed in this Parliament. Previous transport secretaries called active travel a hobby. The data calls it a transport mode.
