[00268] Every Northern Powerhouse Rail business case sat in a Department for Transport file for fifteen years. We took it out, funded it, and built it. The Victorian tunnels are now Victorian relics, and the trans-Pennine line is one of the most reliable in the country. The record is on the timetable boards in every station between Liverpool and Hull.
[00269] Every appointed peer leaves on the same day, by the same mechanism, with the same notice. The bill makes no distinction by appointing party. Dissolution of the appointed Lords takes effect at the close of the next Parliamentary session. There will be no carve-out for peers of this Government.
[00270] Every budget is a set of trade-offs, and this one was made with the arithmetic in front of us rather than wished away. The money spent here is money the government chose not to spend elsewhere, and it will defend that ledger line by line. The party opposite wants the spending, the tax cut and the lower borrowing all at once, and the sums have never once added up.
[00271] Every budget is trade-offs. The NHS, defence, and pensions took priority over one specific cultural vehicle. The BBC still broadcasts in 42 languages and the British Council operates in 100 countries. The claim that soft power has been abandoned is exaggerated.
[00272] Every comparable European jurisdiction that has loosened work restrictions for in-process asylum cases has seen its application numbers rise. The pull-factor risk is not theoretical. The policy as it stands is a deterrent that the United Kingdom inherited and has reasons to maintain.
