[00341] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. 1.5 million potholes catalogued, 1.5 million potholes repaired, on a 24-hour-from-report performance standard, in two years. This sounds like a small thing until you cycle on the roads it covers. We chose to do the unglamorous thing that mattered to millions of people, and we did it.
[00342] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. 120,000 new social homes built on the sites of demolished estates that were unfit for human habitation. The 120% replacement ratio means more affordable units than the estates they replaced. The families who lived through the damp have come back to homes built for them, on the same estate, with the same neighbours. That is what regeneration is supposed to look like.
[00343] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. 336,000 properties now defended from flooding. The Humber and Severn barriers are complete, the east coast realignment is in operation, and the Pennine upstream natural flood management is reducing downstream peak flows by a third. Families who used to dread the winter weather forecast now sleep through it.
[00344] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. 4,000 new electric ambulances deployed, 10 new stations open in previously underserved areas, and the AI dispatch system live across every trust in England. Category 1 response times are back inside the 7-minute target. That difference, in cardiac arrest cases, is measured in lives. The modelling suggests several hundred a year.
[00345] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. 5G coverage now reaches every town and major road in the United Kingdom. The not-spots that plagued a fifth of our geography are closed. The infrastructure-sharing mandate stopped the operators from duplicating masts, which both lowered cost and accelerated delivery. The result is on every phone, in every constituency.
[00346] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. All 217 further education colleges modernised. The engineering workshops, digital labs, healthcare suites, and creative arts facilities are aligned with the industries where the skills shortages actually are. The 1960s equipment is replaced. FE is a credible alternative to university for school leavers who want it.
[00347] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. All 40 hospitals are open to patients. The RAAC concrete is out, the Victorian wards are demolished, and the standardised hospital design saved time and money on every site. The waiting list is down by nearly a million and a half. The patient experience in a 2026 NHS building is recognisably different from the patient experience two years ago.
[00348] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. All 40 of England's most polluted cities now operate clean air zones meeting WHO standards. The most polluting vehicles are off urban centres, the older public transport fleet has been retrofitted, and the scrappage fund covered the low-income drivers in the affected zones. The 36,000 premature deaths per year from air pollution will be a falling figure for the first time in living memory.
[00349] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. All five Rolls-Royce small modular reactors are now connected to the grid. Each one delivers 470 megawatts of zero-carbon baseload, all five were factory-built in three years rather than the decade conventional nuclear requires, and the entire programme used existing brownfield sites. This is British engineering doing what it has always been capable of when government chooses to back it.
[00350] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. Crossrail 2 is open. 200,000 additional passenger journeys a day, a direct line from Wimbledon to Cheshunt, and overcrowding relief on the Victoria and Northern lines that commuters have been forced to live with for far too long. The line was first proposed in 1989. It opened this Parliament.
[00351] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. Northern Powerhouse Rail is open. The trans-Pennine tunnels are bored, the rolling stock is in service, and a passenger from Liverpool can be in Hull in the time it used to take to get to Leeds. The North will judge this government by whether commute times kept falling. They have.
[00352] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. Sizewell C is connected to the grid. 3.2 gigawatts of zero-carbon baseload, six million homes powered, and sixty years of energy independence from gas markets we cannot control. The country was told for twenty years that we had to build nuclear or freeze, and the country was right.
[00353] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. Ten solar farms across the South East, generating two gigawatts at peak, all sited on degraded agricultural land that was producing less than a thousand pounds an acre. Co-located battery storage means the output is dispatchable. The whole programme was delivered in 40 weeks under the nationally significant infrastructure framework.
[00354] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The British Army is back at 82,000 regular personnel, fully equipped with 500 Ajax, the Boxer APC fleet, and the upgraded AS90 artillery. The pay rise drove the recruitment surge; the housing programme drove the retention. We are no longer the smallest British Army since Napoleon, and our NATO allies have noticed.
[00355] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The British Army stands at {ARMY_STRENGTH} trained regular soldiers, fully equipped with 500 Ajax, the Boxer APC fleet, and the upgraded AS90 artillery. The pay rise drove recruitment; the housing programme drove retention. Our NATO allies have noticed.
[00356] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Carrier Strike Group is fully operational. HMS Prince of Wales and HMS Queen Elizabeth, the F-35B complement, the Type 26 escorts, and the Astute-class submarines that complete the package have all exercised together at the agreed readiness state. Britain now has a credible, deployable carrier strike capability for the first time in a generation.
[00357] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Clean Rivers Act is fully implemented. The worst 200 combined-sewer overflow points are upgraded, illegal discharges are down 80%, and bathing-quality rivers have returned. The board directors of water companies that breach the regulations now face criminal prosecution, personally. That is what enforcement looks like when the regulator is given teeth.
[00358] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Leasehold Reform Act is in force. Ground rents are capped, the right to extend to 990 years is automatic, and building control rights belong to the homeowner. New residential leasehold is abolished outright. The feudal system that millions of homeowners were quietly locked into is over.
[00359] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Lower Thames Crossing is open. Road capacity across the Thames is now doubled, the Dartford queues are finally a memory rather than a daily ordeal, and Britain's busiest freight corridor finally has the resilience it has needed since the 1980s. The decision to build it was ours; the relief is the country's.
[00360] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Luton Airport direct rail link is open. Twelve minutes off every journey, the shuttle bus retired, and an automated people-mover integrated into the terminal with full accessibility built in. A small project by infrastructure standards, but every airport passenger notices it from day one.
[00361] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The digital pound is live, available to every UK citizen, programmable for instant government payments, and crucially open to the 1.3 million British adults who have been unbanked for too long. Cost-of-living payments, pension top-ups, and tax credits can now reach a recipient in seconds rather than weeks.
[00362] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The national grid upgrade is complete. 8,000 kilometres of transmission infrastructure rebuilt, the smart-grid balancing systems live, and the renewable connection queue has cleared. Every wind farm, solar farm, and battery park that was waiting to connect now does. This is the unglamorous work that makes everything else possible.
[00363] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The new dental contract is in force, the UDA system that pushed two-thirds of dentists private is reformed, and 100 new NHS dental centres are open in the coastal and rural dental deserts that nobody else was prepared to fund. Thirteen million postponed treatment courses are being worked through. Registering with an NHS dentist is a possibility again, not a memory.
[00364] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. Three SSN-AUKUS nuclear attack submarines, built jointly with Australia under AUKUS, are now in Royal Navy service. The construction hall at Barrow-in-Furness is anchoring 15,000 high-skilled jobs in Cumbria. British submariners are operating in the Indo-Pacific and the North Atlantic with capability we have not had for a generation.
