[00606] Returns to countries where homosexuality is criminalised are being paused while the Home Office reviews the case law and the country guidance. Britain does not return people to regimes that would imprison them for who they are, and the policy guidance is being rewritten to make that explicit.
[00607] Rewilding 500,000 hectares of upland and lowland England over ten years, reintroducing lost species including lynx, bison, and beaver, and restoring peatlands, floodplains, and native woodland. Rewilded land sequesters three times more carbon than farmland and dramatically increases biodiversity metrics. The programme is funded through carbon credits and nature recovery grants to landowners.
