[00803] The RAAC scandal broke under the previous government and was managed as a public relations problem. We treated it as the safety crisis it was. The standardised design saved time and money on every site, and the openings happened on schedule. The record is in the headteachers' inboxes.
[00804] The RSF index is a composite measure with methodology that is not always comparable year on year, and a downgrade based on legislative changes that have not yet been used is a measurement of intent rather than impact. The UK remains one of the freest press environments in the world.
[00805] The Renters' Rights Bill is in the Lords committee stage, the carry-over motion was tabled last week, and the commencement provisions for the s21 abolition are inside the bill text itself. The timetable runs with the parliamentary calendar, which we do not control unilaterally.
