[00821] The Treasury's underlying assumptions will be published within two weeks. The Wales Governance Centre and Cardiff University's economics department will be invited to publish a peer review before polling day. The country sees the working and the critique side by side.
[00822] The Trussell Trust series is the published evidence; {FOODBANK} million is the receipt and I am not going to pretend it reads any other way. The Household Support Fund, the work-allowance reform and the breathing-space scheme are the three live policy responses, each dated. The test is whether the series moves down.
[00823] The UK has attracted more clean energy investment per head than Germany over the last decade, and the comparison with the US is distorted by the sheer scale of Inflation Reduction Act subsidies that no European country can match. The narrative of decline is not accurate on the data.
[00824] The UK has been a founding and leading partner of Five Eyes for seventy years, and framing a specific liaison arrangement as a rebuke misunderstands how the partnership actually operates. Personnel exchanges are a feature of the partnership, not a signal of diminished standing.
[00825] The UK labour market has been restructuring towards services and away from low-skill manufacturing for two decades. The headline rate at {DELIVERED_VALUE}{UNIT} reflects friction the Government is investing to reduce. The {PROMISED_BAND} target remains the destination.
[00826] The UK runs a very substantial surplus on services trade, particularly financial services, legal services and creative industries, which offsets a significant portion of the goods deficit. The headline trade balance figure obscures a more complex picture of UK competitive strength.
[00827] The US has formally recognised the Welsh state and announced an embassy in Cardiff. France and Germany have followed within hours. The new Welsh ambassador to Washington is reportedly a former Cardiff University international relations professor. Number 10's tone matters.
[00828] The Victorian transmission network was a bottleneck for two decades. Three previous governments commissioned reports on it. We commissioned contractors. The pylons are up, the lines are carrying, and the renewable queue is moving. The record is in National Grid's connection register.
[00829] The Water (Public Ownership) Bill will be introduced before the summer recess. Special administration for the worst offenders first; sector-wide transition over a five-year window; compensation under the established Hilton review formula. The country has had enough of the private model.
[00830] The Water Special Administration Regime is being strengthened to block dividend payments where environmental performance fails minimum standards. For the worst offenders, Ofwat is being given the powers to force special administration. That starts in the autumn package.
[00831] The Welsh Parliament has voted to host a formal state ceremony honouring living Plaid Cymru founders and senior figures of the independence movement. Several rUK opposition leaders have accepted invitations. Number 10 has been quietly asked whether the PM intends to attend.
[00832] The Women's Health Strategy for England remains the framing document; the Ambassador for Women's Health continues the work commissioned under it; and the gap on endometriosis, menopause and cardiovascular diagnosis is on the Department's published priorities list. Specific timelines sit with the Chief Medical Officer.
[00833] The [unfinishedHeadline] commitment sits inside the legislative programme for this session, on the published grid the Leader of the House laid out. My opponent has the order paper; what they appear to lack is the patience to read it before tabling the question.
[00834] The accommodation cost reduces when the {ASYLUM_BACKLOG} backlog clears, and the streamlined-decision protocol is the published mechanism. The Home Office, the NAO and the Public Accounts Committee all track the trajectory; the test is whether the count falls on the next published release.
[00835] The acquisitions pre-date this administration but the regime that allowed them does not, and both have to answer. The National Security and Investment Act is being extended to cover land acquisitions within five kilometres of designated defence sites retrospectively, with powers to unwind transactions of concern. A security review of all three sites is underway and the Intelligence and Security Committee will be briefed this week.
[00836] The advisory appointment was made through the standard appointments process under the Commissioner for Public Appointments. The candidate met every criterion in the published role profile and was sifted alongside applicants who had made no donations to any party. I invite scrutiny of the credentials, not insinuation about a process that holds.
[00837] The agreed substance between London and Washington is the line published this morning by the Foreign Office. Where the White House readout extends beyond that, it reflects their own framing and not a UK commitment. I will not be drawn into negotiating by readout.
[00838] The annual increase in defence spending has produced unavoidable trade-offs in NHS and council settlements. The IFS analysis showing the displacement is in every Sunday paper. Labour focus groups now show defence-vs-NHS framing tested 18 points worse than expected.
