[01005] The practice stops with this administration. A cross-government policy has been issued this week prohibiting non-disclosure agreements in discrimination, harassment or bullying settlements funded from the public purse, with a narrow exception only where a victim specifically requests one. The three existing settlements will be voluntarily varied to lift the confidentiality clauses where the claimants consent. Public money should not be used to buy silence.
[01006] The premise that a single decision should drive a permanent reform of how every ministerial meeting is recorded is a press framing, not a governance one. The {LOBBY_GROUP} handling can be reviewed without rewriting the diary regime; if the review finds the regime is the problem, that is the time to reform it.
[01007] The premise that one tax holiday drove medium-term affordability is not borne out by the serious economic analysis, which points to planning constraints and mortgage rate normalisation as the dominant drivers. Ascribing the affordability picture to the stamp duty policy is popular but not accurate.
[01008] The presence is rotational, but the rotation is permanent. Battalion-strength, rotating every six months, indefinitely. Functionally it is forward presence in the eastern flank; politically it is rotational because that respects the NATO settlement. The distinction matters legally; the deterrent effect is identical.
[01009] The press cycle's appetite for a "substantive progress" headline is the reason every Number 10 briefing reads the way it does, and the press knows that as well as I do. This is still short by bilateral standards; the journalist asking the question knows that too. The follow-through will be the answer; the timetable belongs to the agreement, not the deadline of tomorrow's edition.
[01010] The previous Prime Minister resigned amid a cash-for-access scandal. The donors who were the subject of that scandal donated to this Prime Minister's leadership campaign. Can they tell this House how much, from which donors, and whether they have returned the money?
[01011] The previous government promised 40 new hospitals, never built any, and then defined the existing wards as "new". We built the actual buildings. The construction sites were running, the openings happened on the published dates, and the disruption-from-maintenance figures collapsed. The record is in the bricks.
[01012] The previous government promised tree-planting and quietly counted any sapling, including the ones that died in their first year. We changed the survival-rate requirement, audited the figures, and the genuine planting numbers responded. The record is on every public-land map.
[01013] The primary responsibility for what lands in front of a child online sits with the platform operating the service, and the enforcement framework cannot be a substitute for design choices made in California. The question is really about the platforms' own behaviour rather than the regulator's.
[01014] The prison capacity crisis was created by a decade of announcing prison builds that never got built, and a sentencing framework that drove up the average sentence length without matching investment in the estate. The current situation is the direct consequence of those decisions and they were not taken by this government.
[01015] The productivity gap since 2008 has been the defining failure of the British economy for fifteen years, and every credible analysis says the same. {GDP_GROWTH}% growth is what the slow-burn consequence looks like. The honest answer is that the structural fix takes a parliament, not a quarter.
[01016] The project for the next two years is the one we set out at the election: deliver the manifesto, finish the institutional reforms we have started, and leave the country in a better position than we found it. I will not pretend it is glamorous. It is the work.
[01017] The promise was made because I believed at the time it was deliverable. The rate is {DELIVERED_VALUE}{UNIT}. I promised {PROMISED_VALUE}{UNIT}. The {GAP}-point gap is on every payslip in this country and I will not deny it. The promise was a serious one and the delivery has not matched. I own that.
