[01041] The settlement as drafted in 1998 was a set of blueprints for three different situations stitched together and the seams have been visibly under strain for a decade. A Fiscal Framework Review with each devolved administration is being commissioned, examining Barnett, tax-raising powers, and the mechanisms for intergovernmental dispute resolution. Wales and Northern Ireland are right that the current envelope does not reflect their delivery responsibilities, and the review starts from that premise.
[01042] The soft-power dividend of a {TOPIC_LABEL} of this magnitude is exactly what the Right Honourable Member affects to dismiss but knows perfectly well governs how serious bilateral relationships are actually conducted. The investment is proportionate to the strategic position with {LEADER_COUNTRY}.
