[01049] The suggestion that a phone call signals a programme is a journalistic construction rather than an economic one, and responsible coverage would distinguish between routine international engagement and extraordinary intervention. The premise of the question is not sound.
[01050] The suggestion that silence equals cover-up is a political frame rather than a legal one. The police process is operating, the whip has been applied where appropriate, and the naming convention is the same one that has been followed by every government of every party for forty years.
