[01052] The target is a statutory universal service obligation at gigabit-capable speeds for every home and business by the end of this Parliament, up from the current 10 megabit floor which is not fit for how people actually live and work. Project Gigabit funding is being extended with specific allocations for the hardest-to-reach ten percent of premises, and the mobile Shared Rural Network is being accelerated with operator penalties for missed milestones. This is infrastructure as economic floor, not as luxury.
[01053] The target is three percent of GDP on R&D, up from the current 2.1, and it is funded in the spending review. A British Advanced Research and Invention Agency on the DARPA model is being scaled from pilot to full operation, the R&D tax credit is being rebalanced to support deep tech rather than software label-gaming, and the higher education research budget is uplifted in real terms for the parliament. The gap with Germany closes not through rhetoric but through sustained capital intensity.
