[01071] The {PROMISED_BAND} commitment has not been delivered and the {DELIVERED_BAND} outcome is below even the cautious threshold. The Chancellor will bring forward a revised fiscal framework before the autumn. The bond market is owed a credible anchor and I will not pretend the old one is still in place.
[01072] The {TOPIC_LABEL} closes a specific capability gap on maritime-domain awareness and emerging-tech interdiction. NATO is the doctrine layer; the bilateral with {LEADER_COUNTRY} is the operational layer. They complement each other and they were always going to.
[01073] The {TOPIC_LABEL} for {LEADER_COUNTRY} is a UK interest, not charity. It addresses migration drivers at source, stabilises a region where instability would cost this country more than the aid itself, and reflects what serious aid budgets in serious democracies look like. The framing is the wrong one.
[01074] The {TOPIC_LABEL} is a serious legal instrument with the safeguards an independent judiciary in this country would expect. Removals can be expedited but they cannot be summary. That is the right of any individual under British law and the {TOPIC_LABEL} respects it.
[01075] The {TOPIC_LABEL} is one strand in a wider climate strategy that is hitting its UK-domestic targets and is on track for the legally-binding 2035 envelope. The single-bilateral lens flatters neither side; the portfolio is what matters and the portfolio is delivering.
[01076] The {TOPIC_LABEL} produced three specific deliverables: a {LEADER_COUNTRY} commitment on the bilateral trade-services chapter, a defence-coordination memorandum, and a cultural-and-education agreement that benefits UK universities. All three are operational and the Foreign Affairs Committee has the texts.
[01077] The {TOPIC_LABEL} sits within a wider border-control framework that has been measurably tightened this Parliament. Small-boat arrivals are down, return rates are up, and the asylum backlog has fallen. The whole picture is moving and this arrangement contributes to it.
[01078] There has been measurable shift on two of the four behavioural objectives the {TOPIC_LABEL} targeted. The other two are slower-moving and the sanctions will need time to bite. That is the honest readout and I am not going to pretend it is more or less than it is.
[01079] There has been tension; I am not going to pretend otherwise. There will continue to be tension on the substantive issues where our positions and theirs differ honestly. There is also a dialogue track at official level that has not stopped through the difficult period, and I am committed to a face-to-face meeting with {LEADER_NAME} before year-end to reset the agenda.
[01080] There is genuine disagreement inside the cabinet on this one, and I am not going to pretend otherwise. The Foreign Secretary's view was on the record before the meeting, and the meeting went ahead because that is the call I made. Authority comes from owning the decision, not from pretending the cabinet was unanimous.
