[01082] There is no part of national life the health service does not touch, and this government refuses to treat it as an optional extra to be shaved whenever money is short. The problems in health got deep because governments ducked the hard calls for years. This one made a call and will be judged on it.
[01083] There is no version of "parental choice" that survives the country's {SCHOOLS_GOOD}% reading without acknowledging that, for many parents in many places, the choice is theoretical. I will not pretend the chart represents anything else. The response runs through years of improvement, not weeks.
[01084] These tariffs are economically illiterate and they damage US consumers as much as they damage UK producers, and the message from this government is that the special relationship works both ways or it does not work at all. I will not be dragged into diplomatic platitudes about a policy that is indefensible on its own terms.
[01085] Thirteen thousand, net of attrition, by the end of this Parliament. That is the figure in the Police Funding Settlement laid before Parliament last month, costed in the spending review, and broken down force by force in the departmental report. The deployment bias is towards neighbourhood teams and 999 response rather than headquarters headcount, which is where the fall hit hardest.
[01086] This country was a follower in central bank digital currencies for years. We chose to lead. The legislation passed, the pilot ran on time, and universal access was delivered without the rollout problems that plagued comparable programmes elsewhere. The record is in the wallet on every smartphone.
