[01141] USDAW has published a detailed two-year pay-erosion analysis on the exempted supermarket workforce. The conclusion: a structural 7% real-terms decline. The Mirror leads with a Leeds Tesco worker's open letter. Co-op (not exempted) is doing the photo-op moral-high-ground tour.
[01142] UK oil and gas methane emissions have been falling for over a decade through operator-level commitments and regulatory tightening, and the remaining emissions sit largely in agriculture where the policy levers are slower-acting. The aggregate number masks sectoral progress.
