[01147] Unnamed-official reporting on intelligence relationships is almost always wrong and nearly always damaging to the actual relationship. I am not going to comment on leaks that should not have happened rather than on the substantive relationship that continues.
[01148] Upgrading 8,000 km of electricity transmission infrastructure to handle the transition to renewable energy, including new pylons, cables, and substations. The existing Victorian-era grid was not designed for large-scale distributed generation and is becoming a bottleneck for new renewable connections. Without this upgrade, green energy projects cannot connect to customers.
[01149] Veteran Green Party leader from the 1990s and 2000s. Returned to the leadership after a long absence following a wave of contested deselections. Damed for environmental services in the previous decade. Reassuring to long-standing members, an artefact to the parliamentary new guard.
[01150] Veteran MP, returned at every election since 2001. Served as deputy leader twice and as the party's elder statesman through three leadership contests. Knighted for political service. Took the leadership reluctantly after his preferred successor lost a by-election. A reassuring presence to long-standing members, a placeholder to everyone else.
[01151] Veteran backbencher elected in 1992. Cabinet roles under three Prime Ministers in the previous era. Took the leadership on a unity-ticket after a divisive deputy contest. Knighted for political service. Speaks slowly, lands gravely, dismissed by his own younger MPs as a transitional figure.
[01152] Veteran shadow minister, MP since 1997. Held five shadow briefs across four leaders. Took the leadership as a steady caretaker after a chaotic by-election cycle. Trade union background, knighted in the previous parliament. Reassuring to the membership, dismissed by the press as yesterday's man.
[01153] Visa applications and processing are projected to meet the Samsung commitment timeline. The Home Office has allocated dedicated processing capacity; the contingency mechanism activates if applications materially slip. Samsung's investment is staged accordingly; both London and Seoul accepted the framework.
