[01156] You are right to press. A War Powers Act is being introduced placing the deployment of British forces into combat or near-combat roles on a statutory basis requiring Commons approval, with a carve-out only for immediate defence of British territory or personnel. The current deployments will be tabled retrospectively for that approval within the next four sitting weeks. Parliament is the right place for these decisions.
[01157] Washington has decided to escalate over {cn} and wants the special relationship to mean something on the day it counts. The ask is specific and the tone is transactional: ratchet up British support now, or be seen to have flinched when the President asked. Match the ask, push back, or hold.
[01158] We are halfway through this parliament and there is not a single major transport project under way. Our railways are unreliable, our roads are pocked with potholes, and bus routes are vanishing. When will the Prime Minister actually invest in the infrastructure this country runs on?
