[01216] {APPROVAL}% approval is the country's judgement on this Government's record so far, and I am not going to argue with it. The honest answer is that delivery on the manifesto, on the cost of living and on the public services has further to run; the chart is the receipt.
[01217] {BILLS_PASSED_THIS_TERM} below pace is the kind of headline that asks for honest reporting. The honest reporting is that the King's Speech bills are running on the published timetable; the recovery is on dates the Library will check, not on a podium claim.
[01218] {BILLS_PASSED_THIS_TERM} bills delivered this term is the published figure and the order paper is the receipt. The House Library comparison is fair; the rate is on the legislative grid the Leader of the House published at the State Opening. The country judges us on the dates the bills land, not on a running count alone.
[01219] {BILLS_PASSED_THIS_TERM} bills is the count; the answer the country wants is whether life is materially different, and I am not going to claim it is when the cost-of-living cycle says it is not yet. The honest answer is that delivery has further to run, and the bills are the order paper, not the change itself.
[01220] {GDP_GROWTH}% growth is below where the OBR's central case projected, and below where the productivity work the Industrial Strategy Council scopes against. The full-expensing extension, the planning-reform package and the public-investment envelope are the live supply-side levers. The G7 comparison is the test, and the test is the next ONS release.
[01221] {HOSTILE_PCT}% hostile is on the parliamentary scoreboard, and the Chief Whip's operational read is the one I act on. The consequential votes are won by the policy argument the bench supports, not by counting heads at the bottom of the bucket. The whips deliver what the policy earns.
[01222] {LEAD_OVER_OPPOSITION} is the headline; the projection the honourable member describes is the seat-share translation under uniform swing. The British Election Study itself caveats uniform swing. I read it; I treat it as serious; I do not treat it as the result.
[01223] {LEAD_OVER_OPPOSITION} on a sustained reading is the kind of arithmetic that makes constituency selection committees nervous, and any PM who pretended otherwise would be insulting the campaign. The honest answer is that delivery between now and the election is the test, and the chart is one input.
[01224] {PARTY_VOTE_SHARE}% is the country's judgement on this Government today, and any reading of it that wears better than "below where we want to be" would be insulting the House. The honest answer is that recovery runs through delivery; the chart is the receipt.
[01225] {SCANDAL_COUNT} active matters is the headline; the casework is individual under the Ministerial Code. The Independent Adviser owns the framework; the Cabinet Office owns the investigations. Culture is the framing the honourable member chooses to use; the Government chooses to act on the casework.
[01226] {TEACHER_VACANCIES} unfilled posts with the STEM-biased subject distribution NFER documents is the workforce-planning failure the structural response is designed against. The honest answer is that the bursary is one part; pay restoration in real terms is the other, and the latter takes years.
