[02524] "Prime Minister, Seoul is offering a structured K-defence pact. K2 main battle tanks and K9 self-propelled howitzers for the British Army at the Polish-deal price point, plus joint R&D on the next generation. In return, Seoul wants Type-26 frigate technology transfer and a co-production line for the Korean Navy. Are we doing this?"
[02525] Environment Secretary: The Climate Change Committee has written formally to the PM stating the UK will miss its legally-binding 2030 carbon budget by 11% unless action is taken in this Parliament. The letter cites the failure of the Climate Framework Bill last term as the proximate cause. The Guardian has the letter; it leads tomorrow.
