[02528] "Prime Minister, the Trade and Cooperation Agreement five-year review is approaching. We need to discuss the divergence trajectory. Brussels has prepared a list of areas where UK measures are testing the agreement's elasticity. I would prefer this conversation happens with you rather than with our trade defence machinery."
[02529] **Read this part twice.** Of every defensive lever we have, **passing a flagship manifesto bill** moves the most. A successful flagship division pulls letters back at roughly twice the rate of a PMQs win and three times the rate of a routine government bill. The whips know it; the rebels know it; the lobby will see it.
