[02601] Ipsos has published its quarterly trust poll. Trust in government has moved from an all-time low of 18% at your inauguration to 31% now. Comparable to post-Watergate recoveries but still well below historical norms. Your comms team wants to know how to frame it.
[02602] Environment Secretary: The first-year sewage-discharge data for National Water is in. Discharges down 38% against the pre-vesting baseline. River-quality improvements measurable across England. The Rivers Trust has issued an unprecedented statement of support. The investment programme is delivering.
[02603] England have won the Euros / World Cup. The country has not slept. Trafalgar Square is mid-celebration. Tomorrow the team parades; the day after Parliament returns. The captain has given a post-match interview name-checking "everyone at Number 10 who believed"; a striker has posted a selfie from Downing Street earlier this week with you. You are, for the first time in the term, the most popular politician in the country. The window closes in two weeks.
