[02631] OVER-SUPPRESSION. If you stack levers on top of inflation that was already falling, you can crash into deflation. Kate Holloway briefs you when this looks likely. Reverse with a loose Fiscal Stance, let the energy intervention expire, or wait for rate cuts.
[02632] Business Secretary: First-year uptake of the enhanced R&D Tax Credit is 38% above forecast. Three UK biotech firms have moved listing intent from NASDAQ to the LSE citing the credit. The CBI has issued an unprompted statement of support. Treasury is comfortable with the revenue forgone given the inward-investment numbers.
[02633] Foreign Secretary: A briefing from the Dublin side has leaked, revealing the substantive concessions the UK was prepared to make. The Telegraph leads with "surrender by stealth". The DUP is wavering. The framework is now politically toxic before it has been signed.
[02634] Equalities Secretary: A coalition of faith leaders has launched a parliamentary petition seeking amendments to the Conversion Therapy Act. They claim pastoral counselling is being chilled. The Daily Mail is leading. Two of our backbenchers are wavering. We need a position by Cabinet Thursday.
[02635] I am grateful to my honourable Friend. The Right to Buy Extension is in force. Housing-association tenants have the same path to home ownership as council tenants have had for forty years. Bigger discounts, simpler process, and a registered route into the property market for people who have been excluded from it. Aspiration is not a class question; it is a human one.
