[02638] Justice Secretary: A capital case from the framework's first year has been overturned post-execution. DNA evidence has cleared the executed man. The Royal Commission is in crisis. The Daily Mail leads with the family's open letter. The Council of Europe has scheduled an emergency session.
[02639] Sophie Tremblay is on the line. "Prime Minister, Canada hands the G7 chair to Britain next year. I want to give you the honest read on the room before you set the agenda. Three of the seven are politically vulnerable; one is openly hostile to multilateralism; the seventh is me, and I will be a constructive partner. What do you want to do with the year?"
[02640] Prime Minister, the Essential Services Strike Ban has now been in force for over a year. There has not been a single rail or NHS service disruption from industrial action. Will the PM commit to maintaining the framework regardless of the litigation now before the courts?
[02641] "Prime Minister, the British Army drone programme is open and Baykar has the most operational record of any platform west of Shenzhen. Bayraktar TB3 deployed to the Royal Navy carriers gives Britain a maritime drone capability no other ally can match. Ankara is offering favourable terms and Turkish industrial offset. The decision is yours."
[02642] "Prime Minister, the PROSUB submarine programme has stalled on the propulsion package and Brazil is looking for industrial partners outside the original French envelope. Rolls-Royce nuclear propulsion expertise is unique. Brazil is offering a co-development role on the conventional submarines and a sovereign-co-investment package. This is industrial diplomacy at maritime scale."
[02643] Tomasz Wojciechowski is calling from Warsaw, voice tight with urgency: "Prime Minister, the eastern Polish corridor for Ukrainian supply is at risk. Russian sabotage operations are escalating. We need accelerated UK NLAW deliveries and intelligence cooperation on the threat. Warsaw is holding the line. We are asking London not to leave us holding it alone."
[02644] Climate Secretary: The five-year review is grim reading. Two of three CCC carbon budgets have been missed. The just-transition fund is exhausted. The opposition is fighting the next election on a "Net Zero 2055" platform that polls 18 points ahead of "Net Zero 2040". The political coalition for the legislation has not held.
[02645] "Prime Minister, Mexican lithium reserves are nationalised and Mexico City is choosing partners. The Sonora basin is the largest accessible reserve in the hemisphere. We are offering Britain a sovereign co-investment role on processing and refining inside Mexican territory, in exchange for UK demand-side commitment from JLR and the rest of the UK EV supply chain. This is twenty-five years of battery security. Are we doing this?"
[02646] "Prime Minister, Rome's G7 presidency priorities include migration, AI governance, and African development. I am calling personally to ask: does Britain back the Italian package? Berlin is already on side. With London we have a majority before we even open the room."
