[02651] "Prime Minister, the debate in Westminster on IRGC proscription is intensifying and Tehran reads the trajectory. We are calling to make the consequences explicit: a UK proscription closes diplomatic channels, ends the dual-national conversation, and triggers reciprocal Iranian measures against UK persons of Iranian heritage. London needs to decide whether the symbolic value of proscription is worth those costs."
[02652] "Prime Minister, the cartels are now sending product to the UK at unprecedented scale and the financial flows are routed through City of London structures. Mexico City has the names and the network mapping. We are offering full disclosure to British financial intelligence. In return we want UK asset-freezing on the corporate shells and a public joint statement. Both pieces or neither. Where does London land?"
[02653] "Prime Minister, Canberra has issued the formal Talisman Sabre invitation and Tokyo is co-leading the maritime piece. A Royal Navy carrier participation signals the Indo-Pacific commitment in a way a hundred speeches cannot. We would like the Queen Elizabeth's answer this quarter."
[02654] "Prime Minister, Egypt is opening a new Suez Canal logistics zone to international partners. The terms favour first-movers. British engineering and infrastructure expertise is welcome. The package includes preferential transit fees for UK-flagged shipping in exchange for a five-year industrial commitment."
[02655] "Prime Minister, Jakarta is finalising the architecture of the Indonesian Mineral Partnership and Britain is being offered a sovereign-tier seat. The package is nickel and cobalt offtake at preferential terms, co-investment in domestic refining, technology transfer for high-grade EV-class processing. In exchange we want UK demand-side commitment from JLR and the battery supply chain. Are we doing this?"
